## Welcome

> No matter if you are a beginner or an advanced user, starting with Owl is easy.

Owl Carousel 3 is a community-maintained continuation of the familiar touch-enabled jQuery carousel. It preserves the established plugin API, events, markup, and CSS classes while adding jQuery 4 support and a modern build and test setup.

### Features

* Responsive layouts, looping, centering, stage padding, and merged items
* Mouse, touch, RTL, URL hash, autoplay, and callback support
* Lazy loading, auto height, CSS animations, and YouTube/Vimeo video support
* Navigation buttons and dots with customizable markup and containers

### Compatibility

Owl Carousel 3 supports jQuery `>=1.8.3 <5`. The automated browser matrix covers jQuery 1.8.3, 2.2.4, 3.7.1, and 4.0.0, both with and without the matching jQuery Migrate version.

Version 3 keeps the browser-facing Owl Carousel 2 API compatible. If you compile custom Sass themes or upgrade an existing project, read the [jQuery 4 and upgrade guidance](https://github.com/vDyl/OwlCarousel3/blob/main/UPGRADEJ4.md).


### Library

Install the published package with `npm install owlcarousel3`, or download the automatic source archive from the [GitHub releases page](https://github.com/vDyl/OwlCarousel3/releases).

Prebuilt CSS and JavaScript are available in `dist/`; users do not need to run the build themselves.

### Files included

Distributed version structure:

```no-highlight
dist/
├── assets/
│   ├── owl.carousel.css
│   ├── owl.carousel.min.css
│   ├── owl.theme.default.css
│   ├── owl.theme.default.min.css
│   ├── owl.theme.green.css
│   ├── owl.theme.green.min.css
│   └── owl.video.play.png
│
├── owl.carousel.js
├── owl.carousel.min.js
├── LICENSE
└── README.md
```

### Dependency

Load a compatible [jQuery](https://jquery.com/) version before Owl Carousel. jQuery is declared as a peer dependency by the npm package.


